==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|en|pom|y|gloss2=diminutive suffix}}. Australian from 1912.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|pommie}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɒmi/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-pommy.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒmi|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia|New Zealand|South Africa|often derogatory}} A [[pom]]; a person of [[British]] descent, a [[Briton]]; an [[Englishman]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1931|author=[[w:Miles Franklin|Miles Franklin]]|title=Back to Bool Bool|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=YvfPAAAAMAAJ&q=%22pommy%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&dq=%22pommy%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=oDXjT6XhJOatiQfWlrT3Dg&redir_esc=y|page=140
|passage=Though Sir Oswald had taken on enough London veneer to be sneered at as a '''pommy''' in certain Australian circles, he had never acquired the high-class Englishman′s apparent equanimity or indifference before the prospect of cuckolding.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Tony Parsons|title=Silver in the Sun|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=6s73jQWCFnkC&pg=PT115&dq=%22pommy%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=di7jT-KFCuqTiAeWsqCDDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22pommy%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=unnumbered
|passage=Rhona nodded her agreement. ‘That′s a very interesting answer from a new Aussie – and a '''Pommy''' into the bargain,’ she added.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Robert Holman|title=On Paths of Ash: The Extraordinary Story of an Australian Prisoner of War|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=VUynemaVDxMC&pg=PT71&dq=%22pommy%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=di7jT-KFCuqTiAeWsqCDDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22pommy%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=unnumbered
|passage=During one of these acts of bravery by the English pilots I saw a great big tough Aussie with tears of frustration streaming down his face. He was shouting, ‘You magnificent, stupid '''Pommy''' bastard!’}}

